        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: resolve gollaw code health audit findings (#293)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nSystematic code-health and hardening pass for wacli using a stricter local build of\ngollaw, plus targeted refactors in wacli where the findings represented real\nmaintainability, API-surface, duplication, dead-code, or security risk.\n\nThis PR now brings wacli to a clean default gollaw gate:\n\n| Scan | main | This branch |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| Default gollaw | 24 findings: 1 critical, 23 warning | 0 findings |\n| Strict hint scan | 113 findings: 1 critical, 23 warning, 4 info, 85 hint | 2 info only |\n\nThe two remaining strict-mode findings are informational build-tag notices:\n\n- `internal/lock/lock_unix.go`: guarded by `!windows`\n- `internal/syscontacts/other.go`: guarded by `!darwin`\n\nThose are intentional OS-specific files, not code-health issues to remove.\n\nRefs #293.\n\n## Why this is higher quality than main\n\nThis is not just scanner appeasement. The branch improves the codebase in ways\nthat should hold up during normal maintenance:\n\n- removes the critical SQL-construction finding present on `main`\n- breaks up large command/app functions into smaller helpers with clearer\n  responsibilities\n- reduces duplicated mutex/client, send, sync, message, and store patterns\n- narrows internal API surface by unexporting symbols that do not need to be\n  public inside their packages\n- removes or moves dead/test-only production surface instead of suppressing it\n- keeps the default analyzer gate at zero without `//gollaw:keep`, ignores, or\n  relaxed yaml policy\n\nMy judgment: the branch is materially higher quality than `main`, especially for\nmaintainability and security posture. The caveat is that this is a broad\nrefactor across CLI, app, store, and WhatsApp integration paths, so it still\ndeserves careful review and smoke testing even though the static gate and tests\nare green.\n\n## wacli changes\n\n- Refactored large Cobra command constructors and command `RunE` bodies into\n  focused option structs and `run*` helpers.\n- Reduced duplicated send/select/status/sticker/file command plumbing.\n- Extracted repeated sync, backfill, message-store, poll, status, media, and WA\n  client logic into smaller helpers.\n- Tightened unexported/internal types and helper names where they were only used\n  inside one package.\n- Kept OS-specific build-tag files intact as valid platform boundaries.\n- Avoided suppressions and broad configuration softening.\n\n## gollaw-side improvements used by this branch\n\nThe current result depends on the stricter gollaw work that was developed along\nthe way:\n\n- dead-code analysis now tracks main/init roots, generated migration-style\n  registries, cobra command registration, and common Go call/reference shapes\n  more accurately\n- security analysis gives agent-fixable messages and flags real dynamic SQL\n  construction instead of benign error/log formatting\n- thin-wrapper, duplicate-code, large-function, API-surface, unused-member, and\n  feature-flag checks were tightened so they are stricter where it matters and\n  less noisy where Go/framework patterns are intentional\n\n## Verification\n\nLocal verification on this branch:\n\n- `/tmp/gollaw analyze . --format compact --no-suppress`\n  - `TOTAL: 0 findings (0 critical, 0 warning, 0 info, 0 hint)`\n- `/tmp/gollaw analyze . --format compact --min-severity hint --no-suppress`\n  - `TOTAL: 2 findings (0 critical, 0 warning, 2 info, 0 hint)`\n- `go test ./...`\n- `pnpm test`\n- `pnpm build`\n\nMain comparison from a clean worktree at `834c03f`:\n\n- default gollaw: `24 findings (1 critical, 23 warning)`\n- strict hint scan: `113 findings (1 critical, 23 warning, 4 info, 85 hint)`\n- `go test ./...` also passes on main, so the difference is static\n  quality/security/code-health findings rather than basic test pass/fail status.\n\nLive WhatsApp smoke test against Dovocoder / Assistent:\n\n- sent a text message to `Assistent`\n- send returned success with message id `3EB0A09830F04596A2CC3C`\n- `sync --once --idle-exit 20s` connected and exited cleanly\n- local message listing showed the sent probe and an `OK` reply from Assistent\n\n## Review risk\n\nThe result is cleaner than `main`, but the diff is broad: 66 files changed across\nCLI, app, store, and WA integration code. Review should focus on behavioral\ncompatibility for command flags, sync/backfill paths, store migrations, and WA\nsend/media paths.\n",
        "branch": "chore/gollaw-code-health-audit",
